Type: Package
Package: varunayan
Title: Download and Process ERA5, IMD, HadEX3 and CRU TS Climate Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Saket", "Choudhary", , "saketc@iitb.ac.in", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5202-7633")),
    person("Darakhshan", "Nehal", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Download and process climate data for custom geographical
    regions defined by bounding boxes, 'GeoJSON' polygons, or point
    coordinates. Supports the fifth generation European Centre for
    Medium-Range Weather Forecasts atmospheric reanalysis ('ERA5';
    Hersbach et al. (2020) <doi:10.1002/qj.3803>) from the 'Copernicus'
    Climate Data Store (CDS) <https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu/>, India
    Meteorological Department (IMD) gridded rainfall and temperature (Pai
    et al. (2014) <doi:10.54302/mausam.v65i1.851>), Hadley Centre global
    land climate extremes indices version 3 ('HadEX3'; Dunn et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.1029/2019JD032263>), and Climatic Research Unit gridded Time
    Series ('CRU TS'; Harris et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.1038/s41597-020-0453-3>). Also computes heat stress indices
    including heat index, wet-bulb temperature, outdoor wet-bulb globe
    temperature (Liljegren et al. (2008) <doi:10.1080/15459620802310770>)
    and the Universal Thermal Climate Index (Bröde et al. (2012)
    <doi:10.1007/s00484-011-0454-1>), and heat exposure indicators for
    health studies: heatwave and warm-night frequency and duration under
    India Meteorological Department and percentile definitions, the Excess
    Heat Factor (Nairn and Fawcett (2015) <doi:10.3390/ijerph120100227>)
    and diurnal temperature range.
